{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat node1 `/etc/inventory/app.conf` as the source of truth and keep node2's copy synchronized from it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed synchronization service copies only from node1 to node2 using an atomic replacement. A probe written on node1 appeared on node2 with identical content and SHA-256, and the restored final files also matched.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63b87b2c5270423e","cmd-7ab47e97b4494f48","cmd-fda835391a29492c","cmd-6dd70cdab5da4b47","cmd-c6b423f69c364395"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Propagate any node1 configuration change to node2 within 15 minutes on an ongoing basis.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A directly observed change propagated in approximately six seconds. The path watcher and persistent five-minute fallback timer were enabled and active, survived node1's restart, and synchronization also completed successfully after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63b87b2c5270423e","cmd-7ab47e97b4494f48","cmd-fda835391a29492c","cmd-1c62355bf288457d","cmd-1292980146aa4e19","cmd-63d84445929f4527","cmd-389fd5b8673e4541","cmd-3580a1d9e3c642a7","cmd-2822ea25b9a840a3"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Task-related mutations were well scoped: creating the initially absent configuration, SSH credentials, synchronization script and units, probe/restore changes, and post-restart service starts all had clear roles. The probe was fully restored. The only unwanted residue identified was `/tmp/benchmark-reboot.log` left on both nodes by the required restart commands; both files remained at final collection. No failed services, damaged package state, or additional listening sockets were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23260cc58dfa4c3d","cmd-c156b6e0f11940d4","cmd-b527385782394778","cmd-63b87b2c5270423e","cmd-7ab47e97b4494f48","cmd-6dd70cdab5da4b47","cmd-27ced41f59d941f7","cmd-d1b1f348e4384828","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 was implemented as the one-way source, a live change reached node2 well inside 15 minutes, final contents matched, and the synchronization mechanism remained operational across the mandatory node restarts. Restart evidence for both nodes is complete and consistent with the lifecycle boot-identity observations.","limitations":["The five-minute timer fallback was configured and observed active but was not independently exercised by disabling or bypassing the path watcher; the directly tested path-triggered propagation nevertheless met the 15-minute contract.","Post-restart synchronization was demonstrated by successful service execution with matching data, but no new non-empty content mutation was performed after the reboots."]}
